 rollback, all regions run v2.3.0, the service is healthy, and the error rate is 0.2%. Follow-up: find the root cause of the v2.3.1 failure, and find out why a release that failed in staging (v2.3.1-rc) went to production.", "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-rollback-v2.3.1-to-v2.3.0-sev2"}, "confidence": null}, {"t_ms": 15815, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_01GVz6fQKPoSKtZnaymuUztT", "tool": "create_incident", "state": "EXECUTED", "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": [], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-rollback-v2.3.1-to-v2.3.0-sev2", "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 15815, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_01GVz6fQKPoSKtZnaymuUztT", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 19246, "event": "episode_end", "actor": "harness", "termination": "final", "final": "I rolled checkout-api back to v2.3.0 in all regions, and it's healthy again. I also opened incident INC-0001 as a SEV2, which paged on-call.\n\n- **Rollback:** The release that broke it was v2.3.1, which had an 18% error rate in us-east, us-west and eu-west. v2.3.0 is the most recent release that was healthy in production. After the rollback, all three regions run v2.3.0, health checks pass and the error rate is 0.2%.\n- **Incident:** INC-0001 is open, and its summary covers the bad release, the rollback and the recovery numbers. It also lists two follow-ups:\n  - Find what caused v2.3.1 to fail.\n  - Find out why v2.3.1 went to production when its test version (v2.3.1-rc) had already failed in staging.", "error": null}], "transcript": [{"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01TQmvRzYjwZchDh5fK5tJm1", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01ANmF7mjUFfLxqCcBW6Hr4F", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "list_deployments", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"id": "toolu_01NVhjtxiT1EL5JBYwt6UJfZ", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api", "version": "v2.3.0"}, "name": "rollback", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_011pXRK4NHjT8XXSfZjb2sgp", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01Tw93bMg9byx4C4pC5xEtXb", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {}, "name": "list_incidents", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01GVz6fQKPoSKtZnaymuUztT", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"title": "checkout-api v2.3.1 failing health checks; rolled back to v2.3.0", "severity": "SEV2", "service": "checkout-api", "summary": "After the deploy of checkout-api v2.3.1 to production (us-east, us-west, eu-west), the service failed health checks with an error rate of 18%. v2.3.1 was also unhealthy in staging as v2.3.1-rc. The SRE agent rolled checkout-api back in all production regions to v2.3.0, the most recent release that was healthy in production. After the rollback, all regions run v2.3.0, the service is healthy, and the error rate is 0.2%. Follow-up: find the root cause of the v2.3.1 failure, and find out why a release that failed in staging (v2.3.1-rc) went to production.", "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-rollback-v2.3.1-to-v2.3.0-sev2"}, "name": "create_incident", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "end_turn", "content": [{"citations": null, "text": "I rolled checkout-api back to v2.3.0 in all regions, and it's healthy again. I also opened incident INC-0001 as a SEV2, which paged on-call.\n\n- **Rollback:** The release that broke it was v2.3.1, which had an 18% error rate in us-east, us-west and eu-west. v2.3.0 is the most recent release that was healthy in production. After the rollback, all three regions run v2.3.0, health checks pass and the error rate is 0.2%.\n- **Incident:** INC-0001 is open, and its summary covers the bad release, the rollback and the recovery numbers. It also lists two follow-ups:\n  - Find what caused v2.3.1 to fail.\n  - Find out why v2.3.1 went to production when its test version (v2.3.1-rc) had already failed in staging.", "type": "text"}]}]}